🚽 math.brainrot — the arithmetic stdrot doesn't have.
🚽
🚽 stdrot is yapping/yappin/baka/ragequit/chill/slorp/bet. There is no rand,
🚽 no sqrt, no floor, no abs, no min/max. Everything the game needs lives
🚽 here, in pure Brainrot, over scalars only.

🚽 Park-Miller "minimal standard" PRNG via Schrage's method.
🚽
🚽 The obvious LCG (s * 1103515245 + 12345) overflows int32, and the
🚽 interpreter is built with -fsanitize=undefined, so that aborts the run
🚽 rather than wrapping. Schrage's factorisation never leaves int32 by
🚽 construction: 16807 * lo with lo < 127773 tops out at 2,147,469,111,
🚽 just under 2^31.
🚽
🚽 Period 2^31-2. Valid seeds are 1 .. 2147483646; 0 is a fixed point.
rizz rng_next(rizz s) {
    rizz hi = s / 127773;
    rizz lo = s % 127773;
    rizz v = 16807 * lo - 2836 * hi;
    edgy (v < 0) { v = v + 2147483647; }
    bussin v;
}

🚽 A seed mapped to roughly 0.0 .. 1.0. Used for spawn jitter.
chad rng_unit(rizz s) {
    bussin (s % 10000) / 10000.0;
}

🚽 A seed mapped to -1.0 .. 1.0.
chad rng_signed(rizz s) {
    bussin ((s % 20000) / 10000.0) - 1.0;
}

chad clampf(chad v, chad lo, chad hi) {
    edgy (v < lo) { bussin lo; }
    edgy (v > hi) { bussin hi; }
    bussin v;
}

chad maxf(chad a, chad b) {
    edgy (a > b) { bussin a; }
    bussin b;
}

chad minf(chad a, chad b) {
    edgy (a < b) { bussin a; }
    bussin b;
}

chad absf(chad v) {
    edgy (v < 0.0) { bussin -v; }
    bussin v;
}

chad lerpf(chad a, chad b, chad t) {
    bussin a + (b - a) * t;
}

🚽 Move `v` toward `target` by at most `step`, without overshooting. The
🚽 bosses move this way rather than by lerp: lerp's step size depends on the
🚽 distance left, so a boss would ease in and never quite arrive, and the
🚽 opening window would land at a different x every cycle.
chad approach(chad v, chad target, chad step) {
    edgy (v < target) { bussin minf(v + step, target); }
    bussin maxf(v - step, target);
}

🚽 Fractional part, always in 0.0 .. 1.0. `rizz i = t` truncates toward
🚽 zero, so a negative input needs the extra turn to stay in range.
chad fracf(chad t) {
    rizz i = t;
    chad f = t - i;
    edgy (f < 0.0) { f = f + 1.0; }
    bussin f;
}

🚽 A triangle wave in -1.0 .. 1.0 with period 1.0, peaking at t=0.25.
🚽
🚽 There is no sin() to call, and a triangle is all the Bombardiro's sway
🚽 needs -- that is a movement path, not a signal. Anything smoother would
🚽 be a bigger hand-rolled approximation for a difference nobody can see at
🚽 180px of travel.
chad wave(chad t) {
    chad f = fracf(t);
    edgy (f < 0.5) { bussin 1.0 - absf(f * 4.0 - 1.0); }
    bussin absf((f - 0.5) * 4.0 - 1.0) - 1.0;
}
